flowchart TB
  accTitle: DorkOS systems and deployment boundaries
  accDescr: The DorkOS client reaches a local execution server. Community has its own browser, server and storage. Cloud is optional. The website and local installer both read marketplace sources. The remote-community connection is unfinished.
  client["DorkOS client · React<br/>Browser / phone web app / desktop"]
  subgraph local["Your machine or self-hosted environment"]
    server["DorkOS server · Express<br/>Sessions · Rooms · Tasks · Relay · Mesh<br/>Local SQLite + files"]
    runtime["AgentRuntime implementations<br/>Claude Code · Codex · OpenCode<br/>Runtime-specific history"]
    server -->|"SDK calls / local sidecar"| runtime
  end
  subgraph independent["Independent Community deployment"]
    communityUI["Community browser · React"]
    community["Community server · Hono<br/>Own sign-in · PostgreSQL · blob storage"]
    communityUI <-->|"HTTP commands / SSE events"| community
  end
  cloud["DorkOS Cloud · optional<br/>Public contract<br/>Service under development"]
  sources["Marketplace sources<br/>Registries + package repositories"]
  site["DorkOS website · Next.js<br/>Docs + marketplace discovery"]
  client <-->|"HTTP commands / WebSocket events"| server
  server -.->|"Local app connection in development<br/>HTTP + SSE"| community
  server -->|"Optional HTTPS<br/>Link, heartbeat, managed services"| cloud
  server -->|"Fetch packages<br/>HTTPS / Git / npm"| sources
  site -->|"HTTPS metadata + READMEs"| sources
  classDef service fill:#edf3fa,stroke:#46709b,color:#183047
  classDef developing fill:#fff5e4,stroke:#a87720,color:#49320c
  class server,community,runtime,client,communityUI,site,sources service
  class cloud developing
